      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's practical effects and CGI integration set new standards for mid-budget sci-fi. The prawns' design feels unnervingly real, while the mechanical suits and weapons showcase the perfect blend of alien tech and industrial grit. This approach influenced later films like <a href=\"/movie/137113\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"137113\">Edge of Tomorrow</a> (2014) and <a href=\"/movie/43933\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"43933\">Monsters</a> (2010), proving you don't need $200 million to create convincing otherworldly creatures and technology."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's exploration of corporate exploitation and military contractors draws clear parallels to films like <a href=\"/movie/5548\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"5548\">RoboCop</a> (1987) and <a href=\"/movie/19995\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"19995\">Avatar</a> (2009). Multi-National United's ruthless treatment of both aliens and humans echoes themes from <a href=\"/movie/8337\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"8337\">They Live</a> (1988), while the transformation horror elements recall <a href=\"/movie/9426\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"9426\">The Fly</a> (1986). SUBHEAD: Impact on Modern Sci-Fi"
      },
